# =================================================================================================================================================================
# NOTES:
# - the synthesis may fail because the oracle gets hit by an output vector which is not corret, enable Z3 to debug
# - if the 'incremental learning' is active and the oracle returns a wrong hit, the e-graph is wrongly updated
# - ignoring the variables classification and using Z3 to spot the equivalent classes leads to even better results, at the cost of heavy slowdown due to Z3 proving
# =================================================================================================================================================================
# TODO:
# - implement the LLVM-based simplification of the e-classes (based on 'llvmlite') => it's missing some passes, most notable EarlyCSE!
# - implement the GAMBA-based tricks to enhance the simplification of the e-classes
# - add a better temporary variables support to handle things like: `((sub-tree)^const)|const` that is equivalent to `sub-tree|const`
# - cache the e-class evaluation done by SiMBA and avoid processing it again
# - mark the e-class as potentially equivalent in SiMBA if the QSynth cost is not being used (maintain a global cache)
# - detect non-linear expressions and exclude them from SiMBA (for safety, although always replacing constants with variables is much safer already)
# - after using Z3 to determine the relations between the constants, add these relations to the e-graph (hoping it'll lead to better optimisations)
# - after simplification group all the symbolic variables that appear next to other symbolic variables to reduce the total amount of variables (BITWISE-EXAMPLE)
# - apply SiMBA on pure symbolic expressions using only boolean operations (as QMC or ESPRESSO or sympy)
# - apply the Groebner Bases boolean minimization approach on boolean subtrees (https://github.com/cispa/Microarchitectural-Hash-Function-Recovery/)
# =================================================================================================================================================================

